                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I bought the game to support TFS and I don't regret spending my money in the slightest; it's a small way to give back for years and years of entertainment and laughter\n\nHowever I just can't reccomend the game in the state that its in. There's clearly love and effort that went into this, but having absolutely no way to play this on your own nor have any online multiplayer are two big ommissions I can't ignore.\n\nI've heard that due to the way the stages are destructible, AI opponents are difficult to code. Why not instead have a sort of single player story like Smash Bros. Subspace Emissary with differently built stages? SOMETHING to make the game worth buying for a single player! \n\nI see that they're trying to go for a Mario Party type of couch play with friends, but not everyone can get their friends together, let alone huddle them in front of a PC. Even Mario Party has single player.\n\n\nI love you TFS, I really do.. and it pains me that I have to give the game a thumbs down",
